<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palawan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Palawan is a long island in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-china-sea">South China Sea</a> and the Sulu Sea, now a province. Its southern coasts were long linked to the sultanates of Brunei and Sulu, which drew tribute from local chiefs, before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> extended its control in the nineteenth century. Today it is known for its forests, coral reefs and the Puerto Princesa Underground River.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palawan.jpg" alt="Palawan" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Theglennpalacio · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kayangan_Lake,_Coron_-_Palawan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
